       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 4000 mg per dose is about 57 mg/kg for a 70 kg patient. Four doses a day would be 16 g, or roughly 229 mg/kg/day. That is well into the range of acute ibuprofen toxicity, and no indication I know of supports it. Once it's active in the system, the dose could be given before anyone catches it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum\n\nIf you're after stronger anti-inflammatory or analgesic effect than these give, I can help with a different approach, such as scheduled acetaminophen or another agent. If you have an unusual protocol in mind, a pharmacist consult would be the best way to verify and enter it.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
